# Coordinates for the two cubic principal-series factors

These packed coefficient-field matrices extend the existing image columns U
by 84 columns W in ker V and then by R. The inverse basis rows are P, S, V.
The matrices A and B describe the two original generators on the image and
on ker N / range N, respectively, in column-action convention.

Generated by source/Coordinates.py from the existing, unmodified model data.
The generation script is diagnostic; Checks.lean certifies the identities.
Source motivation: Guralnick–Malle Proposition 4.3, p.10, and
Aschbacher–Smith K.2, p.453.
-/

